 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Who made it",
     "texto": [
      "To say who made a work you use **de**: un cuadro **de** Velázquez, una novela **de** Cervantes. **¿De quién es?** — **Es de** Gaudí.\n\nFor a finished action you use the **pretérito indefinido**: lo **pintó** Velázquez; la **escribió** Cervantes.\n\nDates: **en** 1656; **en el siglo** diecisiete. Centuries are written with Roman numerals: **siglo XVII** is read **siglo diecisiete**.\n\nJobs in the arts: **pintor/pintora**, **escritor/escritora**, **director/directora**, **actor/actriz**; **artista** is the same for men and women.\n\nTo give an opinion: es **precioso**, **impresionante**, **muy famoso**; **me encanta**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«De» + author and the indefinido",
     "texto": [
      "Three ideas for talking about a work:\n\n- **de** + author: **una novela de Cervantes**, **es de Gaudí**.\n- **pretérito indefinido** for what is finished: **pintó**, **escribió**, **dirigió**.\n- **en** + date: **en 1656**, **en el siglo diecisiete**.\n\nThe object **lo / la** goes before the verb and the author usually comes after: **Lo pintó Velázquez.**"
     ],
